<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Random Joke Generator</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: sans-serif;
      text-align: center;
    }

    #joke-container {
      margin-top: 20px;
      font-size: 1.2em;
      color: red; /* This line changes the color to red */
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <h1>Random Joke Generator</h1>

  <button id="joke-button">Tell Me a Joke!</button>

  <div id="joke-container">
    <!-- Joke will appear here -->
  </div>


  <script>
    const jokes = [
      "Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!",
      "Why did the scarecrow win an award? Because he was outstanding in his field!",
      "Parallel lines have so much in common. It’s a shame they’ll never meet.",
      "Why did the bicycle fall over? Because it was two tired!"
    ];

    const jokeButton = document.getElementById("joke-button");
    const jokeContainer = document.getElementById("joke-container");

    jokeButton.addEventListener("click", function() {
      const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * jokes.length);
      jokeContainer.textContent = jokes[randomIndex];
    });
  </script>

</body>
</html>
```

**Explanation:**

The key change is adding the following line inside the `<style>` section within the `<head>`:

```css
#joke-container {
  /* ... other styles ... */
  color: red;
}
```

* **`#joke-container`:** This CSS selector targets the HTML element with the ID "joke-container" (which is the `<div>` where the jokes are displayed).
* **`color: red;`:**  This CSS property sets the text color of the element to red.

Now, whenever a joke is displayed in the `joke-container` div, it will be rendered in red.  This is the simplest and most direct way to achieve the desired color change using CSS.

